  "query_preview": "..\nAn upper level disturbance moving east across eastern Montana\ntoday will help bring showers and thunderstorms east across the\nnorthern zones through this evening. Amounts this evening could \nbe a quarter of an inch in the northeast zones.\n\nWinds will diminish tonight as skies clear and the atmosphere\ndecouples. Then a warm front moves east through Wednesday with \nsome clouds associated with it. High temperatures will be about 5 \nto 10 degrees warmer than today's.\n\nA warmer day is expected Thursday as a cold front approaches the\narea from the northwest. Sunshine and prefrontal compressional \nwarming should allow for temperatures to reach the 80s most \nplaces. With increasing west winds, minimum humidity in the teens \nand little rainfall in the southeast zones recently (tenth of an \ninch or less), a Fire Weather Watch has been issued for Thursday\nfrom noon till 8 pm.\n\nThe cold front then drops southeast across the area Thursday night\nbringing the chance of showers by Friday and temperatures about 15\nto 20 degrees cooler than Thursday.\n\nThe cooler/wetter conditions linger through the weekend as an\nupper trough settles in then an upper low drifts east from the \nPacific NW.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nPops through this evening were tweaked from the NBM to match\nbetter with neighboring offices. Temps Thursday were tweaked\ncloser to NBM90 given the full sun and prefrontal compressional\nwarming. All other elements closely followed the NBM. TFJ",
